@*
    Upload-and-ingest feedback for the three Import Release tabs, shown at the
    top of the form while a submit is in flight. object-explorer-import.js
    drives it through the data-oe-import-* hooks: the bar runs determinate while
    bytes upload, then drops its value attribute to go indeterminate for the
    server-side parse.

    Hidden until the JS unhides it, so a no-JS submit never shows an empty
    banner. The same markup was copied into all three tabs before PR 17c; this
    is the third caller, which is where it becomes a component.
*@

<div class="alert alert--info oe-import-progress" data-oe-import-progress hidden
     role="status" aria-live="polite">
    <div class="oe-import-progress__body">
        <div class="oe-import-progress__row">
            <span data-oe-import-label>Uploading...</span>
            <span class="oe-import-progress__pct" data-oe-import-pct></span>
        </div>
        <progress class="oe-import-progress__bar" data-oe-import-bar max="100" value="0"></progress>
        <p class="oe-import-progress__hint" data-oe-import-hint></p>
    </div>
</div>
